From: =?UTF-8?q?L=C6=B0u=20Oa=20Oa?= <212658678+luuoaoa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 21 Aug 2026 02:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] update_engine: serve scaled DLC images from colorburst's host

Scaled-DLC installs go through InstallAction, which hardcodes Google's CDN
(edgedl.me.gvt1.com / dl.google.com). colorburst ships a DLC that is not on
that CDN (edk2-ovmf-dlc), so its install 404s and Crostini fails right after
termina; and the Google-hosted DLCs (termina) would still be fetched from
Google, contrary to de-Googling. Point the four hardcoded DLC URLs at
colorburst's own host (dl.colorburst.net). The image is verified against the
on-device imageloader manifest image_sha256, so this needs no separate
signing -- the hosted object must be the exact dlc.img built for the running
OS version. This is a superset replacement for the reverted factory-install
approach (which could not survive OTA or powerwash).
---
diff --git a/update_engine/cros/install_action.cc b/update_engine/cros/install_action.cc
index 82e623e170..4669ae4446 100644
--- a/update_engine/cros/install_action.cc
+++ b/update_engine/cros/install_action.cc
@@ -31,11 +31,20 @@
 namespace chromeos_update_engine {
 
 namespace {
-constexpr char kBandaidUrl[] = "https://edgedl.me.gvt1.com/edgedl/dlc";
-constexpr char kLorryUrl[] = "https://dl.google.com/dlc";
-
-constexpr char kBandaidArtifactsMetaUrl[] = "https://edgedl.me.gvt1.com/edgedl";
-constexpr char kLorryArtifactsMetaUrl[] = "https://dl.google.com";
+// colorburst: scaled-DLC installs go through this action, which hardcodes
+// Google's CDN. A colorburst-specific DLC (e.g. edk2-ovmf-dlc) is not on that
+// CDN, so it 404s and Crostini install fails right after termina; and even the
+// Google-hosted DLCs (termina) would be fetched from Google, which the fork is
+// meant to avoid. Serve every DLC from colorburst's own host instead. The
+// downloaded image is verified against the on-device imageloader manifest
+// image_sha256 (see OnTransferComplete below), so no separate payload signing
+// is required -- the object hosted must be the exact dlc.img built for the
+// running OS version. Same host for primary and backup (we run one origin).
+constexpr char kBandaidUrl[] = "https://dl.colorburst.net/dlc";
+constexpr char kLorryUrl[] = "https://dl.colorburst.net/dlc";
+
+constexpr char kBandaidArtifactsMetaUrl[] = "https://dl.colorburst.net";
+constexpr char kLorryArtifactsMetaUrl[] = "https://dl.colorburst.net";
 
 constexpr char kUrlNameBandaid[] = "<BANDAID>";
 constexpr char kUrlNameLorry[] = "<LORRY>";
